-- expect: 15:3: the body of this `for` performs an operation that resumes (the operation 1.0), and its source `&a` lends `a` around the whole loop: an operation that resumes cannot cross a borrow (T1, #172). Iterate an owned array, or a view the function is given
-- rejected today; intended to run: pending #172, corpus/pending/hard-gen-owned-yields-refs.bc
-- A `for` over `&a`, whose body performs `yield`. `&a` lends `a` for the whole loop (SPEC §9,
-- §16), and the loop is div because its body performs an operation that resumes: the
-- continuation of `yield` would hold the lend across a suspension, which is T1 (#172). Over the
-- owned array, or over a view the generator is given, the same loop runs
-- (`corpus/for-data-div.bc`).

include yield

fn tab(i: i32) -> i32 = i + 1

fn elems_of() -> 1 with Yield[i32] =
  let a = array_new[i32] (3, tab);
  for x in &a { yield(*x) };
  ()

main -> i32 =
  let mut acc = 0;
  for x in elems_of() { acc = acc + x };
  acc
